 "title": "How Modern Millionaires Build Brands on Attention",
 "topic": "business ideas",
 "summary": "The creator discusses how modern entrepreneurs build wealth by going where attention lives instead of building traditional brick-and-mortar stores. The main lesson is to place your content where people already look, like social media, and monetize it through branded merchandise.",
 "key_points": [
  "Garfield became famous because comics were free in every newspaper, which is where people's attention already was.",
  "The creators of Garfield made billions of dollars by selling t-shirts and mugs, not by charging for the comics.",
  "Gen Z entrepreneurs are not building physical comic book stores; they are appearing where the attention is.",
  "The single greatest advantage in business is existing where all the attention lives, which is social media, and then building a brand to leverage it.",
  "Nobody goes out of their way for a comic book store, but people will not skip content if it is already in their hands."
 ],
 "content": "Video by bitterbuilds. Transcript: A few days ago, a legendary entrepreneur we don't go to the comic book store, but if the comics were in the newspaper, we'd read them. This quote genuinely shifted my perspective on how the next generation of millionaires is being made. Cause here me out, Garfield was free in every newspaper, which is how millions came to recognise it, they made their billions from selling t shirts and mugs like the genius Gen Z Entrepreneurs are not building comic book stores, they are simply appearing in the newspaper. The single greatest advantage is existing where all the attention lives, which is social media, and then building a brand to leverage it. Cause the thing is, nobody goes out of their way for a comic book store, but they won't skip it if it's in their hands.",
